<translate>

{{Caption|A ControlPoly6 generated from a six point line sketch.}}

==Usage==

# There are several options for a preselection:
#* Select one [[Image:Workbench_Sketcher.svg|16px]] [[Sketcher_Workbench|Sketch]] in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]] or in the [[3D_View|3D View]] containing a wire of 5 straight line segments.
#* Select two extended "Node sketches" in the Tree View or in the 3D View, each containing a circle, a straight line starting at the circle center, and a second line starting at the endpoint of the first line.
#* Select two CubicCurve_4 objects connected at one end — this produces a G2 blend.
#* Select one CubicCurve_4 object — this produces an exact match in ControlPoly6 format.
# There are several ways to invoke the command.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_ControlPoly6.svg|16px]] ControlPoly6}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Silk → [[Image:Silk_ControlPoly6.svg|16px]] ControlPoly6}} option from the menu.
# One of the following objects is created:
#* A '''ControlPoly6_5L''' object if the first preselection option was chosen.
#* A '''ControlPoly6_2N''' object if the second preselection option was chosen.
#* A '''ControlPoly6_??''' object if the third preselection option was chosen.
#* A '''ControlPoly4_??''' object if the last preselection option was chosen.
# Optionally adjust parameters in the [[Property_View|Property View]].
# A '''ControlPoly6''' object, is created.

== Properties ==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

All '''ControlPoly6''' objects are derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherits all its properties. They also have the following common additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Weights|FloatList}}: Weights.
* {{PropertyData|reverse|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the parameter direction.

{{Properties_Title|C2 - Outputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Legs|Part::PropertyGeometryList}}: Control segments.
* {{PropertyData|Poles|VectorList}}: Poles.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


A  '''ControlPoly6_5L''' object also has the following individual additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Sketch|Link}}: Reference Sketch.
* {{PropertyData|tolerance|Float}}: Default is {{value|1e-06}}. Point-to-point connection tolerance for the 5 lines.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|ControlPoly6_5L}}. The workbench class used to create this object.


A  '''ControlPoly6_2N''' object also has the following individual additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Sketch0|Link}}: Reference Sketch.
* {{PropertyData|Sketch1|Link}}: Reference Sketch.
* {{PropertyData|tolerance|Float}}: Default is {{value|1e-06}}. Point-to-point connection tolerance for the circle-line in each node.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|ControlPoly6_2N}}. The workbench class used to create this object.


